course: dictionary
lesson: 6882
title: Overreacting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To overreact means to react much more strongly than you need to, such as getting very angry or upset over something small. The prefix over- is a clue: it means too much, so overreact means to react too much.
explain: Here is a sentence about feelings: «Don't overreact, it was an accident.» The word accident tells you nobody meant it, so the best answer is calm, not a huge shout. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "react too much" still makes sense.
explain: Science texts use the word too. «A food allergy is the immune system overreacting to a food, and even a tiny amount can cause a reaction.» The body's defence system reacts far too strongly to food that is harmless, so the reaction is much bigger than it should be.
explain: Look for the phrase «a bit of an overreaction». The noun overreaction is the big reaction itself. Overreacts and overreacted follow the same meaning, so once you know one form, you know them all.
fact: «Overreact» is a verb: I overreact, she overreacts, we overreacted, they are overreacting.
fact: «Overreact» means to react much more strongly than you need to.
fact: The prefix «over-» means too much, as in overcook and overfill.
fact: «Overreaction» is the noun: it is the big reaction itself.
fact: In a food allergy, the body's defence system overreacts to a harmless food, so always tell an adult straight away if you feel unwell after eating.
exercise: «Don't overreact, it was an accident.» What does overreact mean here? | React calmly and kindly | Forget that it ever happened | *React much more strongly than the accident needed | Run away from the accident
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «A food allergy is the immune system overreacting to a food» that shows the body reacting too strongly. | food | *overreacting | allergy | system
exercise: Ben shouted and stamped over a tiny scratch. Priya says, "He's overreacting." What does she mean? | He did not react at all | He was asleep and did not notice | *He reacted much more strongly than the scratch needed | He reacted exactly the right amount
test: «It was only a small joke, so there is no need to overreact.» What is the best meaning of overreact here? | To tell the joke to everyone | To forget the joke straight away | To laugh much too loudly | *To react much more strongly than the joke needed
test: Which part of overreact tells you it means too much? | un- | pre- | *over- | re-
exam: «She had a bit of an overreaction when the bus was late.» What is an overreaction? | *A reaction much bigger than the situation needed | An apology for a small mistake | A rash on the skin | A calm, sensible answer to a problem
